ication difficulty may affect safety-critical communication.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility high, problem solving, concentration, handles unexpected events, but weak leadership, moody (crew cooperation maybe affected). Moodiness could affect stress resilience and cooperation.\n\nCandidate A: technical competence high, anticipates danger, leadership good, but unorganized (reliability) and unfriendly (crew cooperation). Unorganized may affect reliability; unfriendly may affect crew.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate D: strong responsibility, problem solving, concentration, handles unexpected events, but weak leadership and moody. However leadership may be less critical than reliability and stress resilience. Moodiness could be issue.\n\nCandidate B: strong reliability and stress, but uncooperative and pretentious could be severe for crew.\n\nCandidate C: good crew atmosphere, decision quality, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be problematic.\n\nWe need to argue. I think Candidate D may be the best overall because strengths cover many criteria: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, handling unexpected events (stress resilience). Weak leadership and moodiness are concerns but may be mitigated. Others have more severe cooperation issues.\n\nThus I will propose Candidate D as current recommendation, citing evidence.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: none, but we can say \"Given the lack of prior discussion, I propose...\"\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
